{"data":{"updated_timestamp":"23/10/2026 20:16:19","profile":{"player_id":"85064","last_updated":"23/10/2026 20:16","fullname":"Rinitha Rajith","short_display_name":"R Rajith","name":"Rinitha Rajith","gender":"F","dob":"13/01/2006","date_of_death":null,"place_birth":"United Arab Emirates","nationality_id":"19","nationality":"United Arab Emirates","nationality_short_code":"UAE","nick_name":null,"player_skill":{"id":"1","text":"Batsman","role":"Batter"},"batting_style":{"id":"1","text":"Right Handed"},"bowling_style":{"id":"12","text":"Right-arm medium fast"},"writeup":"<p>Born on January 13, 2006, in Ajman, Rinitha Rajith represents one of the most exciting young batting talents to emerge from the United Arab Emirates. Part of a remarkable cricketing family alongside her sisters Rithika and Rishitha, Rinitha quickly developed an attacking flair that separated her from her peers. Right-handed and naturally aggressive, she showed a refreshing fearlessness at the crease from the moment she first picked up a bat in local academies.</p>\r\n<p><br />\r\nRinitha made her senior T20 international debut in March 2022 against Qatar in Oman, immediately catching the eye with her positive intent and clean ball-striking. Her breakthrough on the world stage came during the inaugural ICC Under-19 Women's T20 World Cup in South Africa in 2023. As a key top-order batter, she recorded one of the highest strike rates among Associate players in youth T20 cricket, registering two crucial half-centuries and finishing among the tournament leaders in sixes.</p>\r\n<p><br />\r\nTransitioning into a regular middle-order enforcer for the senior UAE team, Rinitha added versatility to her game by occasionally bowling medium-fast overs and fielding sharply in crucial positions. While many Associate batters focused primarily on survival against top-tier bowling attacks, Rinitha consistently looked to score, using lofted drives and powerful pull shots to disrupt opposition fielding plans.</p>\r\n<p><br />\r\nThe year 2025 saw Rinitha broaden her skill set into the 50-over arena during UAE's international tours of Zimbabwe and Papua New Guinea. She proved that her aggressive style could be adapted to longer formats, constructing a well-paced half-century with a top score of 59 and providing vital middle-order stability. Her contributions in both ODI matches and the GCC T20 Championship highlighted her growing tactical awareness and endurance.</p>\r\n<p><br />\r\nIn 2026, Rinitha produced several impactful performances across Asian cricket tournaments, including a blazing innings of 31 runs off just 17 balls against the Philippines in the ACC Women's T20 Premier Cup in Malaysia. She also played key roles in high-stakes matches during the DP World Asia Cup Rising Stars tournament in Thailand and the senior Women's T20 Asia Cup in Dubai, reinforcing her status as a dependable crisis manager and match finisher.</p>\r\n<p><br />\r\nBy mid-2026, with over sixty senior T20 appearances to her name before turning twenty-one, Rinitha Rajith has already achieved a remarkable foundation in international cricket. Her aggressive approach has set a new benchmark for modern batting in UAE women's cricket. As the sport continues to expand globally with more franchise opportunities and ICC events, Rinitha stands poised to become one of the most celebrated batters in Associate cricket history.&nbsp;</p>","relation":[{"id":85058,"name":"Rithika Rajith","relation":"Sister","relation_id":6},{"id":85065,"name":"Rishitha Rajith","relation":"Sister","relation_id":6}],"social_details":{"social_platform":[{"social_platform_id":"1","social_platform_name":"facebook","social_platform_url":""},{"social_platform_id":"2","social_platform_name":"twitter","social_platform_url":""},{"social_platform_id":"3","social_platform_name":"instagram","social_platform_url":"https://www.instagram.com/_rinitharajith_/"},{"social_platform_id":"4","social_platform_name":"youtube","social_platform_url":""},{"s